	<entry name="Tyranids/TyranidPrime" value="Tyranid Prime"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/TyranidPrimeDescription" value="Fearsome synapse hero unit that boosts allied Tyranid Warriors. <br/><br/>This Unit can be build in the Predator Lair"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/TyranidPrimeFlavor" value="Tyranid Primes are the apex of the Tyranid Warrior strain, faster, stronger and smarter than the other Warriors they lead to battle, who instinctively emulate their deadly skill."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/HiveCrone" value="Hive Crone"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/HiveCroneDescription" value="Flyer unit that excels against airborne targets."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/HiveCroneFlavor" value="The Hive Crone is a flying monstrosity used by the Tyranids to establish air superiority over prey worlds. It is a creature perfectly adapted to aerial combat, able to wrestle enemy aircraft out of the skies as proficiently as any daredevil pilot at the controls of a sophisticated jet-fighter."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/Tyrannocyte" value="Tyrannocyte"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/TyrannocyteDescription" value="Monstrous creature that transports units to the frontline and supports them by pinning down enemy units."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/TyrannocyteFlavor" value="Normally acting as organic drop pods discharged from orbiting Hive Ships, Tyrannocytes have been adapted by the Gladius Prime Hive Mind, isolated as it is by warp storms. Here they act as lumbering floating transports, carrying creatures as large as Carnifexes and protecting them until close to the enemy. Then the Tyrannocyte’s gravid belly opens, disgorging their monstrous cargo, whilst it assaults the enemy with endless barbed stranglers…"/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/Tyrannocyte" value="Tyrannocyte"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/TyrannocyteDescription" value="Monstrous creature that transports units to the frontline and supports them by pinning down enemy units."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/TyrannocyteFlavor" value="Normally acting as organic drop pods discharged from orbiting Hive Ships, Tyrannocytes have been adapted by the Gladius Prime Hive Mind, isolated as it is by warp storms. Here they act as lumbering floating transports, carrying creatures as large as Carnifexes and protecting them until close to the enemy. Then the Tyrannocyte’s gravid belly opens, disgorging their monstrous cargo, whilst it assaults the enemy with endless barbed stranglers…"/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/Malanthrope" value="Malanthrope"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/MalanthropeDescription" value="Support unit that consumes tiles and founds new cities."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/MalanthropeFlavor" value="Malanthropes are rarely seen Tyranid creatures. This is because they are not truly warrior organisms, and so are not usually encountered by a prey world's defenders. Instead, these floating creatures follow behind the Tyranid attack; they are typically created only after a prey world's protectors have been defeated and the swarm is in the process of devouring the planet's biomass. On those few occasions that a survivor has seen a Malanthrope and somehow escaped, they have brought with them a tale of horror. They report seeing these giants drift across corpse-strewn battlefields, but unlike other Tyranids, which mindlessly devour everything in their way, Malanthropes seem to selectively search through the slain—as to what they are searching for, none can say."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationRegeneration" value="-Bio-Adaptations: Regeneration"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationRegenerationDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation regenerate 2 HP per turn. Each Tyranid unit has bio-adaptation slots that limit the number of bio-adaptations it can evolve."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationRegenerationFlavor" value="Torn flesh knits together with sickening speed as adaptive cells multiply beyond mortal comprehension. Wounds that should be fatal become mere inconveniences to the Hive Mind's perfected organisms."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationAdrenalGlands" value="-Bio-Adaptations: Adrenal Glands"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationAdrenalGlandsDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation gain 1 additional Movement. Each Tyranid unit has bio-adaptation slots that limit the number of bio-adaptations it can evolve."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationAdrenalGlandsFlavor" value="Adrenal glands saturate their host's bodies with chemicals that boost the creature's metabolism to a hyperactive state of frenzy."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationToxinSacs" value="-Bio-Adaptations: Offensive Mutations"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationToxinSacsDescription" value="Grants access to the Toxin Sacs and Hunter-Worm Hive bio-adaptations, which increase either melee or ranged capabilities."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationHunterWormHive" value="-Bio-Adaptations: Hunter-Worm Hive"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationHunterWormHiveDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation additional Ranged accuracy. Each Tyranid unit has bio-adaptation slots that limit the number of bio-adaptations it can evolve."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationHunterWormHiveFlavor" value="Writhing clusters of predatory parasites nest beneath chitinous plates, their microscopic senses attuned to distant prey. When the creature fires, a thousand hunter worms guide each projectile with unerring precision."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationAcidicCarapace" value="-Bio-Adaptation: Defensive Carapaces"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationAcidicCarapaceDescription" value="Grants access to the Acidic Carapace and Sporeburst Carapace bio-adaptations, which increase either melee or ranged defense."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationBroodleechHive" value="-Bio-Adaptation: Brood-leech Hive"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationBroodleechHiveDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation apply a damage over time effect and the pinning debuff but suffer from reduced Hitpoints"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationBroodleechHiveFlavor" value="Blood Leech Hives are swollen nodules teeming with parasitic broodleeches, writhing just beneath the creature’s carapace. When the host rends its prey, these vermin spill forth, burrowing into flesh and gnawing it from within, spreading agony and paralysis. Yet the infestation comes at a cost—the Tyranid’s own body is sapped by the constant drain of its loathsome passengers, leaving it more fragile than its kin."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationSwollenBioChambers" value="-Greater Bio-Adaptation: Swollen Bio-Chambers"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationSwollenBioChambersDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation gain 1 additional Range."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationSwollenBioChambersFlavor" value="These grotesquely distended organs swell with volatile fluids and compressed spores. With each convulsive discharge, the swollen chambers hurl living ammunition far beyond its usual reach, saturating distant prey in a storm of bio-organic fire."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationGreaterRegeneration" value="-Greater Bio-Adaptation: Greater Regeneration"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationGreaterRegenerationDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation regenerate 5 HP per turn and gain additional maximum hitpoints."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationGreaterRegenerationFlavor" value="Through hyperactive metabolic nodes and ever-dividing flesh, the beast reknits torn muscle and seals gaping wounds within moments. Even grievous injuries serve only to feed its relentless renewal, as if the Hive Mind itself refuses to let its organism die."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationVampiricSymbiote" value="-Greater Bio-Adaptation: Vampiric Symbiote"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationVampiricSymbioteDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation gain lifesteal with melee weapons and increased melee accuracy."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationVampiricSymbioteFlavor" value="Vampiric symbiotes infest the host’s claws and fangs, each a leech-like organism that hungers for warm ichor. As the Tyranid rends its prey, these parasites drink deep, feeding vitality back into the beast and driving it into a frenzy of ever-more precise strikes."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationEnhancedSenses" value="-Bio-Adaptation: Enhanced Senses"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationEnhancedSensesDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation gain extra sight Range and additional ranged accuracy."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationEnhancedSensesFlavor" value="The beast’s sensory nodes bloom with alien precision, perceiving every movement, every vibration, every heartbeat of its prey."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationFleshHooks" value="-Bio-Adaptation: Flesh Hooks"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationFleshHooksDescription" value="Units with this bio-adaptation gain additional melee attacks and movement after attacking."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationFleshHooksFlavor" value="From hidden recesses in the beast’s thorax erupt fleshy hooks tipped with razored barbs. These organic grapnels find purchase in prey and terrain alike, wrenching the Tyranid into the fray with terrifying momentum. Few foes survive long once the hooks sink home."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationCorrosiveStrikes" value="-Bio-Adaptation: Corrosive Strikes"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationCorrosiveStrikesDescription" value="Grants access to the Corrosive Strikes bio-adaptation, which causes attacks to apply stacking armour-reducing debuffs. Melee attacks shred armour faster."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationCorrosiveStrikesFlavor" value="The swarm learns. Every blade grows teeth, every gland turns caustic, and the prey's proud armour becomes nothing more than a delay."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationLimit" value="Hypermetamorphic Plasticity"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationLimitDescription" value="All Tyranid units gain 1 additional bio-adaptation slot."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/BioAdaptationLimitFlavor" value="The Hive Mind's grasp of this world's biology is now total. Its creatures' flesh becomes endlessly mutable, accommodating ever more elaborate combinations of weaponised organs."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/DeployBroodHive" value="Deploy BroodHive"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/DeployBroodHiveDescription" value="Deploys a Broodhive, a fortification which serves as a Tunnel."/>

	<entry name="Tyranids/SubterraneanAssault1" value="Subterranean Assault 1 / 2"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/SubterraneanAssault1Description" value="Subterranean Assault on all units cost 25 % less influence. Brood Hive tunnels will be equiped with a Stranglethorn Cannon"/>

